				\begin{document}$$\eta t$$\end{document}ηt to, say, a quadratic rise ηt2, one would get h ~ exp(αt2) instead of the Gompertz law. Biologically, the rise of production rate with age may represent the accumulation of damage producing units (DPUs) that are not removed. The DPUs are produced at a constant rate and therefore their number grows linearly with age. Each DPU produces damage, and thus the total damage production rate rises linearly with time.

The production parameter η varied by seven orders of magnitude between species. The longer the lifespan, the lower the η (Fig. 3a). The other model parameters show smaller trends and generally decrease more mildly with lifespan (Extended Data Fig. 1 and Extended Data Tables 2 and 3).Fig. 3Production parameter is the best single predictor of lifespan.
